## Part 3

> yes, make that change then start Phase 3

Strategy step 3: build the Next.js dashboard against the static JSON.

Shell commands run:

    cd .. && mv app/public .scaffold_tmp/public   # keep the generated crm.json
    npx create-next-app@latest app --typescript --tailwind --eslint --app \
        --src-dir --use-npm --no-import-alias --no-turbopack --disable-git --yes
    cp -r .scaffold_tmp/public/data app/public/data && rm -rf .scaffold_tmp
    cd app
    npm i recharts@latest
    npx shadcn@latest init -d -y
    npx shadcn@latest add card tabs table separator -y
    npm run build

Stack: Next.js 16 (App Router, client-rendered page), React 19, Tailwind v4,
shadcn/ui (base-nova / Base UI), recharts 3. Single page, six views, one segment
toggle + year selector, all KPIs recomputed in the browser from customers[].

> I checked the dashboard ... data for months that havent passed yet in 2026 ...
> 70% of leisure customers are one-time ...
> do all three: retune to ~30%, 2026 YTD, add baseline context

Reworked generate.py and the app:
  1. Retuned the repeater model (concentrated bursts confined to one year, B2P
     repeaters skew concentrated, ~4% of customers now cross-year) so the yearly
     repeat rate sits near 30%: 2026 31.7% / B2P 18.6%, 2024-2025 ~34-36%.
  2. 2026 is now year-to-date through 31 Aug 2026 (snapshot date). No data after.
     YoY for 2026 compares Jan-Aug vs Jan-Aug 2025; the app labels it "year-to-date".
  3. Headline now shows the one-time count and the 30% lifetime baseline next to
     the orange rate. Cohort view dims + labels off-peak / too-recent cohort rows.

    uv run python generate.py        # re-run after the retune
    npm run build

> please verify everything, if the data is accurate and provide feedbacks

Full verification pass (QA A-E). Client-side KPI computation matches the JSON
kpis block exactly for all 9 segment x year cells. Found the winter-holiday
volume bump had gone weak after the retune; lifted Nov/Dec month weights and
deepened the October trough so Nov-Dec recover visibly. Re-ran the generator.

    uv run python generate.py

