## Part 5

> Yes please! Use one free openrouter agent as well

Strategy step 5: the chat assistant. Added:
  - app/src/app/api/chat/route.ts  - the only backend logic. Reads meta + the
    precomputed kpis block from public/data/crm.json, builds a compact system
    prompt (no customer array), calls OpenRouter server-side. Missing key -> 503.
  - app/src/lib/chat-context.ts    - the summary builder.
  - app/src/components/dashboard/chat.tsx  - the panel (suggestions, message list).
  - app/.env.local                 - OPENROUTER_API_KEY + OPENROUTER_MODEL
    (minimax/minimax-m3:free), copied from the repo-root .env; git-ignored.
Also added a one-line MoM caption in the headline (Aug vs Jul is post-peak).

    cp ../.env app/.env.local        # then edited to keep only the OpenRouter vars
    npm run build
    curl -s -X POST localhost:3000/api/chat -d '{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"..."}]}'

> the chatbot should be kind of a chat on the side, always visible, not in the
> bottom... most numbers on the Trend are negative, should this be the case?
