## Restyle - Sixt fonts + dark theme

> change the fonts as well to match whatever SIXT is currently using? Also
> explore how you could use the colors to be more dark mode and fancy ... only
> HTML/CSS max, dont change anything else on the data structure or dashboards
> structure and logic

Presentation only - no data, KPI logic or component structure changed.
  - Type: Jost (next/font/google) everywhere - an open geometric sans in the
    Futura / Neue Plak family, the closest Google-hosted match to Sixt's
    corporate face. Loaded as --font-jost, composed into --font-sans /
    --font-heading in globals.css. Card titles bumped to semibold.
  - Theme: committed dark. globals.css :root now holds a warm near-black palette
    (page #0b0a09, card #151310, ink #f4efe9) with Sixt orange #ff5f00 kept exact
    as the single accent. data-theme="dark" fixed on <html>; @custom-variant dark
    keys off it. Faint orange radial bloom behind the header; cards get a
    top-lit gradient + hairline highlight + soft shadow; the orange repeat-rate
    number gets a soft glow (.sixt-accent). Chat bubble is now orange.
  - lib/palette.ts chart colours re-pointed to the dark set (warm off-white
    neutral series, white-opacity grid); recharts legend/tooltip/cursor colours
    updated inline. Hard-coded black/white in cohort, chat, primitives,
    chart-tooltip and the sticky header swapped to tokens.

    npm run build        # clean; typecheck clean

