## Data retune - 2024 repeat rate

> core repeat conversion rate is similar on 2024 and 2025, can you do less on
> 2024. also verify all the data and provide feedback

generate.py weights only - no structural or KPI-logic change.
  - FIRST_YEAR_ONE_TIME  2024 0.28 -> 0.30, 2025 0.31 -> 0.30 (2024 intake
    tilted toward one-timers).
  - FIRST_YEAR_CONCENTRATED  2024 0.29 -> 0.27, 2025 0.32 -> 0.33, 2026 0.21 ->
    0.24 (repeater acquisition shifted from 2024 into 2025; 2026 lifted so its
    Jan-Aug first-rent YoY stays positive against the higher 2025 base).
  - New asserts: 2025 rate - 2024 rate >= 0.025 and 2024 All rate <= 0.345.
  - Result: All Repeat Conversion Rate 2024 34.2% / 2025 38.0% / 2026 31.4% YTD
    (was 36.6 / 36.7 / 30.2 - now a visible upward step). Gross volume 1278 /
    1603 / 1813 / 1363; every displayed YoY still positive. Docstring +
    assumptions.yearly_vs_lifetime_rate / growth reworded: 2024 reads lower
    because that year's fast acquisition growth was one-timer-heavy.

    uv run python generate.py        # all asserts pass
    # + scratchpad/verify.py: 40,350 independent re-derived checks, 0 failures

> Can you please apply the recommendations? Also, verify if theres anything
> needed to change in the pdf after this changes.

Applied the feedback from the previous step (generate.py weights only):
  - rec 1 (2024 gross jump was +25%): raised 2023 one-time weight; 2024 growth
    now +22%, with a new assert gv[2024]/gv[2023] <= 1.25.
  - rec 2 (2025 first-rent YoY was a thin +2.9%): raised 2025 one-time weight ->
    2025 first-rent YoY now +6.8%.
  - rec 3 (2025 rate was 38.0%, near the ceiling): trimmed 2025 concentrated
    weight -> 2025 rate 36.7%; new assert rate_2025 <= 0.375.
  - rec 4 (bimodal repeat gaps): unchanged - it is the spec's fixed 60-90 /
    330-365 band, a documented simplification, not a regression.
  Final: All Repeat Conversion Rate 34.6% / 36.7% / 32.6% YTD; gross 1281 /
  1569 / 1774 / 1412; every displayed YoY positive; step assert relaxed to
  >= 1.8pp. Docstring + assumptions text refreshed (2024 ~35%, 2025 ~37%).

One-pager (docs/repeat-rate-onepager.html) refreshed for the new figures and
re-published to the same artifact URL:
  - blended rate 30.2% -> 32.6% YTD; "held near 30%" -> "runs a few points above
    ... trending up"; "grows ~15%/yr" -> "grows double digits".
  - Channel Breakdown callout: B2P 19% -> 21%, B2C 41% -> 44%, B2P one-time
    81% -> 80%; hypothesis projection 19%->26% becomes 21%->29%.
  - Engagement reach 38% -> 39%. 70% / 2,800 and the 60-90 / 330-365 clusters
    unchanged (still exact).

    uv run python generate.py        # asserts pass
    uv run python scratchpad/verify.py   # 40,266 checks, 0 failures
    npm run build                    # clean

> Can you add a way to see all years together? ... All Time. Also ... Quarters
> ... multiselect ... Before implementing let me know the technical implications
> ... [then] I accept the recommendations. Please implement

Assessed first (quarterly repeat-rate swings 48-63% are window-length + season
artifacts, not retention; full multi-select breaks YoY/MoM/cohort). Implemented
recommendations 1-3 only:

  1. "All Time" period option (4th button, single-select). Pools 2023-2026.
     - lib/crm.ts: ALL_TIME sentinel + YearSel type + isAllTime / yearLabel.
     - lib/kpis.ts: every year-keyed fn takes YearSel; all-time = no year filter,
       no YoY/MoM, population = all customers (rate = 30.0% exactly).
     - headline: hides the Trends grid, relabels; the one-time count line now
       states "this IS the 30% lifetime rate".
     - cohort: 12 rows pooled by first-ever-rental calendar month - a fuller
       retention curve per month (the 6-12mo / 12mo+ columns gain real signal).
     - generate.py: build_kpi_block adds an "all_time" cell per segment; new
       asserts (all-time All = 0.30, below every yearly rate, gross = sum).
  2. Monthly / Quarterly toggle on the headline contract chart only (local
     state, toQuarterly() rollup, partial-quarter caption). Retention metrics
     stay at year / all-time granularity by design.
  3. "All Years at a Glance" card (components/dashboard/trend.tsx): 2024/2025/
     2026 side by side (not summed) - Gross Volume + Repeat Rate mini-charts,
     a dashed lifetime-rate reference line, selected period highlighted.

  Assumptions panel + chat context updated (all_time_view, quarterly_view;
  chat can now answer about the All Time pool). Data unchanged (same seed).

